.TH EUCLID-CLI-EQS-DELETE-QUEUE 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eqs-delete-queue \- delete a queue
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eqs delete-queue
.BR \-\-queue | \-q
.I NAME|ERN
[\fB\-\-if\-empty\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Deletes a queue identified by its Euclid resource name (ERN), along
with all of its remaining messages. This cannot be undone.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-queue " " \fINAME|ERN\fR
Name or ERN of the queue to delete. Required.
.TP
.B \-\-if\-empty
Delete the queue only if it is empty. The request is refused with
.I "HTTP 409"
while the queue holds any message, or while events are still being
delivered into it from a topic subscription. Without it, the queue and
all of its messages are deleted.
.PP
The queue may be given by
.B name
instead of by ERN, in which case it is resolved in your session's account
and namespace; see
.B NAMES AND ERNS
in
.BR euclid-cli-eqs (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The queue was deleted. No output is printed.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, no queue
with that name or ERN exists, or
.B \-\-if\-empty
was given and the queue is not empty.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eqs delete-queue \e
    --queue orders
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eqs (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-create-queue (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-purge-queue (1)
